                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Diagnose the system, not the symptom`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `Eighteen months of demand, production and service data are on the table. A +38% January surge dropped <strong>on-time delivery to 81%</strong> (target 96%) and triggered <strong>$240K in penalties</strong>; then a panic doubling of production left <strong>$3.1M of excess stock (~52 days vs a 30-day target)</strong>. Before you spend a dollar of the $6M budget, diagnose the <strong>system behaviour</strong>: external seasonality is ±40%, but a static plan and reactive ordering added a self-inflicted layer on top. Which lever — capacity, information or buffers — fixes the <em>cause</em>, and which feedback loop turns a stockout into the next glut?`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Set capacity under volatile demand`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `A third anchor client offers a <strong>$14M / 2-year contract</strong> — but it needs <strong>+20% capacity</strong> and tighter service, on a plant already missing 96% at 81% OTD. Average utilization is only <strong>78%</strong>; the +38% peak was a one-month, weather-driven spike. A permanent third line/shift is high fixed cost carried across eleven slow months; <em>flexible capacity</em> (overtime, temp lines, contract mfg) absorbs peaks without the drag. Size capacity to a <strong>demand distribution and a service level</strong>, not to a point forecast or last month's headline — and decide the contract go/no-go.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Choose the digitalization investment`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Allocate the <strong>$3.0M digital slice</strong> across four investments through an Industry 4.0 lens. <strong>Demand-sensing / S&OP</strong> and a <strong>supplier control tower</strong> are information-centric — they attack the bullwhip and the resin-risk blind spot. <strong>MES + line sensors</strong> add real-time OEE visibility. An <strong>automated warehouse</strong> adds throughput. The binding constraint here is decision quality and visibility, not raw speed: <em>technology that improves the signal and the decision often beats technology that only runs faster.</em> And define the decision process it enables — a real S&OP cadence, or the same monthly spreadsheet with prettier dashboards?`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Redesign buffers and defend the plan`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Close the loop. Reset safety stock toward the <strong>30-day target</strong> — a flat policy over-stocks the steady QSR items and under-protects the ±40% export items, the worst of both, so size it <strong>statistically by item</strong>. Manage the <strong>single-sourced resin</strong> (6-week lead time, 3-week delay flagged): dual-source, a sized strategic buffer and revised contract terms — don't just optimize finished goods and leave the upstream risk open. Then set the <strong>KPI scorecard</strong> — OTD, inventory cost, utilization, cost-per-unit together — and ask the hard question: would this plan absorb a repeat +38% peak, or amplify it?`,

                    r1_root_label:          `What is the ROOT cause behind the missed quarter — the lever that addresses the cause, not the symptom?`,
                    r1_split_label:         `How much of the chaos is SELF-INFLICTED variability vs true external demand swing? (% self-inflicted)`,
                    r1_split_readout:       `Share you attribute to your own decisions:`,
                    r1_split_hint:          `External seasonality is ±40%, but over-ordering, batch sizing and a static safety stock added a layer of variability on top of it.`,
                    r1_loop_label:          `Name the feedback loop you most need to break.`,
                    root_system:            `A static plan plus reactive ordering amplifies normal volatility — the bullwhip is self-inflicted; better information and buffer discipline damp it`,
                    root_capacity:          `Not enough capacity — the plant simply can't make enough; add a line and the problem goes away`,
                    root_badluck:           `Bad luck — a freak pineapple season and a competitor outage; nothing systemic, ride it out`,
                    root_supplier:          `The resin supplier — one unreliable vendor is the whole story; everything else is downstream noise`,
                    loop_bullwhip:          `The over-react / over-correct loop — a stockout triggers over-ordering, which becomes a glut, which triggers cuts (the bullwhip)`,
                    loop_penalty:           `The penalty loop — focus only on the clients charging late fees`,
                    loop_none:              `There is no loop — each event was independent and unrelated`,

                    r2_contract_label:      `The USD 14M / 2-year contract requires +20% capacity and tighter service. Go or no-go?`,
                    r2_mix_label:           `How do you source the capacity to handle peaks? (% from PERMANENT new line/shift vs flexible)`,
                    r2_mix_readout:         `Permanent capacity share:`,
                    r2_mix_rest:            `· rest is flexible (overtime / temp lines / contract mfg)`,
                    r2_mix_hint:            `Average utilization is only 78%; the +38% peak was a one-month, weather-driven spike. Permanent capacity is fixed cost carried across eleven slow months.`,
                    r2_service_label:       `Size capacity to a point forecast, or to a demand DISTRIBUTION and a chosen service level?`,
                    contract_conditional:   `Sign, but only conditional on first stabilizing service and sourcing the +20% the right way`,
                    contract_signnow:       `Sign it now — USD 14M is too big to pass up; we'll find the capacity somehow`,
                    contract_decline:       `Decline — we can't serve today's volatility, so don't add a demanding anchor client`,
                    service_distribution:   `To the distribution — pick a service level (~95%) and size cushion + flexibility to meet it cost-effectively`,
                    service_point:          `To the point forecast — plan to the single most-likely demand number`,
                    service_peak:           `To the absolute peak — staff so we never, ever miss, whatever the cost`,

                    r3_alloc_label:         `Allocate the digitalization slice of the budget across the four investments (must total $3.0M)`,
                    r3_total_readout:       `Digital budget allocated:`,
                    r3_total_cap:           `/ $3.0M`,
                    r3_process_label:       `What decision process does the technology actually enable?`,
                    alloc_sop:              `Demand-sensing / S&OP analytics — better signal, attacks the bullwhip (information-centric)`,
                    alloc_tower:            `Supplier-integration / control tower — lead-time & supply-risk visibility (information-centric)`,
                    alloc_mes:              `MES + line sensors — real-time OEE and capacity visibility (mixed)`,
                    alloc_auto:             `Automated finished-goods warehouse — faster throughput, more storage (throughput-centric)`,
                    process_sop:            `A real S&OP cadence — replace the spreadsheet with a weekly demand-and-supply review that acts on the new signal`,
                    process_reports:        `Better month-end reports — same cadence, prettier dashboards`,
                    process_none:           `Nothing changes — install the tools, keep planning on the monthly spreadsheet`,

                    r4_safety_label:        `Redesign safety stock toward the 30-day target. Flat policy, or item-differentiated?`,
                    r4_resin_label:         `Response to the single-sourced compostable-resin risk (6-week lead time, 3-week delay flagged).`,
                    r4_scorecard_label:     `Set the KPI scorecard you will manage to going forward.`,
                    r4_conviction_label:    `Conviction in your integrated two-quarter operating plan — would it absorb a repeat +38% peak? (%)`,
                    safety_statistical:     `Statistical, item-differentiated — size to each SKU's demand variability & lead-time risk (volatile export items vs steady QSR)`,
                    safety_flat:            `One flat safety-stock level across all SKUs — simplest to run`,
                    safety_cut:             `Slash all safety stock hard to hit 30 days fast — inventory is the enemy`,
                    resin_dualsource:       `Dual-source + a sized strategic buffer + revised contract terms — manage the upstream risk directly`,
                    resin_stockpile:        `Just stockpile resin — pile up a huge strategic buffer and call it solved`,
                    resin_ignore:           `Leave it — the finished-goods buffer is optimized; the supplier is a separate problem`,
                    scorecard_balanced:     `Balanced — OTD, inventory cost, capacity utilization and cost-per-unit together`,
                    scorecard_otdonly:      `On-time delivery only — service is all that matters; ignore the cost side`,
                    scorecard_costonly:     `Cost-per-unit only — drive cost down, service will follow`,

                    warn_split_range:       `The self-inflicted share must be a percentage between 0 and 100.`,
                    warn_mix_range:         `The permanent-capacity share must be a percentage between 0 and 100.`,
                    warn_alloc_negative:    `Digital-budget allocations cannot be negative.`,
