                    insight_stabilized:     `System stabilized: you diagnosed the bullwhip instead of chasing the headline, flexed capacity to the distribution, spent the digital budget on the signal, and redesigned buffers statistically with the resin risk managed. Capacity, information and buffers now work together — a repeat +38% peak gets absorbed, not amplified.`,
                    insight_exposed:        `Volatility amplified: the loop is still cracking. Either the bullwhip was never damped or the single-sourced resin risk is still open — one upstream disruption or one peak and the plant whipsaws again, exactly the cycle that started this crisis.`,
                    insight_short:          `You moved the numbers but didn't fully integrate the plan. Capacity, information and buffers still tell slightly different stories — enough that the next peak finds the seam.`,
                    insight_overbuilt:      `Overbuilt and idle: you bought permanent capacity to never miss a peak, and now you carry fixed cost across slow months with utilization below 75%. That's expensive insurance against last month's headline, not a fix for volatility.`,
                    insight_resin:          `The single-sourced resin risk is still open. A 6-week lead time, a flagged delay, and no dual-source means one upstream disruption idles your optimized plant — the low-frequency, high-impact risk you underweighted.`,
                    insight_service:        `On-time delivery is still below 90% and short of the 96% target. The penalty clauses and client-churn risk that started the crisis are still live.`,
                    insight_servicemet:     `On-time delivery is back at or above the 96% target — the service gap that triggered the penalties is closed.`,
